## Three.js discipline (required now)

- **One renderer per component instance** — no shared global renderer
- **Lazy import** `three` — never module-scope in SSR paths
- **Dispose** geometry, material, texture, renderer in disconnect/unmount
- **Pause RAF** when offscreen — use `IntersectionObserver`
- **Clamp DPR:** `Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2)`
- **Resize observer** on container — update camera aspect + renderer size

## Parity status

Full Three.js: WC, React, Angular on `3d-geo-globe`. Svelte/Vue stubs are **grandfathered debt** — close with parity ticket, do not add new stubs.

Per-framework 3D binding (exports):

| Framework | Preferred binding |
|-----------|-------------------|
| React | R3F or direct three (existing pattern) |
| Angular | three.js canvas in component |
| Vue | TresJS when enhancing beyond CE-host |
| Svelte | Threlte when enhancing beyond stub |
| WC | imperative three in CE |

## Geo map

- Provider via prop: `maplibre` (default), `leaflet`, `google-maps`
- Map SDKs as peerDependencies + dynamic import
- Keyboard-accessible marker list fallback (`13-accessibility.mdc`)

## WebXR roadmap (design rules)

When implementing headset support:

- Feature-detect `navigator.xr` — never assume VR hardware
- **Non-VR fallback mandatory** — same data/actions via list/table UI
- Session lifecycle: `requestSession` → render loop → `end` with full dispose
- Controller input mapped to documented public events — not app-private globals
- Do not require WebXR for core dashboard functionality

## Builder preview

3D preview adapters: create/dispose renderer on node change; pause when panel hidden; single animation loop per preview panel (`docs/17-component-plugin-sdk.md`).

## ui-primitives helpers

`map-globe-markers.ts`, `map-scatter-points.ts` — convert preview rows to marker/scatter formats; use in Storybook and builder preview, not in consumer apps directly.

